From: Hannes Reinecke <hare@suse.de>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 11:33:02 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] net/handshake: kABI fixes for handshake status
Patch-Mainline: Never, kABI fix
References: bsc#1273136,CVE-2026-64523

Commit 6b22d433aa13 ("net/handshake: Pass negative errno through handshake_complete()")
changed the 'status' field from 'unsigned int' to 'int', which broke the kABI.
Fix it up to use the original type if kABI checking is activated.

Signed-off-by: Hannes Reinecke <hare@suse.de>
Acked-by: Petr Pavlu <ppavlu@suse.cz>
---
 net/handshake/handshake.h | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/net/handshake/handshake.h b/net/handshake/handshake.h
index da61cadd1ad3e..1ae29ab81714c 100644
--- a/net/handshake/handshake.h
+++ b/net/handshake/handshake.h
@@ -59,7 +59,11 @@ struct handshake_proto {
 	int			(*hp_accept)(struct handshake_req *req,
 					     struct genl_info *info, int fd);
 	void			(*hp_done)(struct handshake_req *req,
+#ifndef __GENKSYMS__
 					   int status,
+#else
+					   unsigned int status,
+#endif
 					   struct genl_info *info);
 	void			(*hp_destroy)(struct handshake_req *req);
 };
@@ -88,8 +92,13 @@ struct handshake_req *handshake_req_hash_lookup(struct sock *sk);
 struct handshake_req *handshake_req_next(struct handshake_net *hn, int class);
 int handshake_req_submit(struct socket *sock, struct handshake_req *req,
 			 gfp_t flags);
+#ifndef __GENKSYMS__
 void handshake_complete(struct handshake_req *req, int status,
 			struct genl_info *info);
+#else
+void handshake_complete(struct handshake_req *req, unsigned int status,
+			struct genl_info *info);
+#endif
 bool handshake_req_cancel(struct sock *sk);
 
 #endif /* _INTERNAL_HANDSHAKE_H */
-- 
